  "question": {
    "text": "A fair die is thrown <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> number of times. If the probability of always getting a number greater than the previous number is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>54</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is equal to <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
